---
code: K0026
title: Mixed Pipes
severity: ERROR
since: 0.1.0
category: parse
deprecated: False
tags: [parse, syntax, pipe, operator, precedence]
description: "'|>' and '<|' pipes cannot be mixed without parentheses"
---

Forward pipes (`|>`, left-associative) and backward pipes (`<|`, right-associative) cannot be mixed in the same expression without explicit parentheses.

## Example

This error occurs when `|>` and `<|` appear at the same grouping level:

```kura
let result = x |> transform <| input
```

## Solution

Add parentheses to make the evaluation order explicit, or rewrite the pipeline using a single pipe direction:

```kura
let result = (x |> transform()) <| input

let consistent = input |> transform(x, _)
```
